WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:01.520
Okay.

00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:05.800
I have a big update for you today about a
truly incredible story that I brought to you

00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:06.800
yesterday.

00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:08.080
Let me catch you up.

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:13.400
Tuesday night we did a live commentary stream
of the democratic presidential debate.

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:15.590
We did it on our Twitch platform.

00:00:15.590 --> 00:00:17.860
We are on all sorts of different platforms.

00:00:17.860 --> 00:00:23.860
We tend to do the live debate coverage on
Twitch, twitch.tv/david Pakman.

00:00:23.860 --> 00:00:29.570
About halfway through that debate, our stream
was shut down along with the streams of numerous

00:00:29.570 --> 00:00:31.290
other left-wing streamers.

00:00:31.290 --> 00:00:35.790
Basically at the same time, almost at the
exact same time now because of the debate

00:00:35.790 --> 00:00:44.370
was on CBS, the assumption was CBS shut down
these debate streams, but very quickly something

00:00:44.370 --> 00:00:50.880
didn't seem quite right and we started to
to to get emails that said that the claimant

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:52.670
was not CBS.

00:00:52.670 --> 00:00:57.770
It was instead a company called Praxis political
legal.

00:00:57.770 --> 00:01:03.330
We did an investigation and immediately we
found that the email address listed as the

00:01:03.330 --> 00:01:10.289
contact email for these claims by PRAKSIS
political legal didn't exist and when I emailed

00:01:10.289 --> 00:01:12.640
them, the email instantly bounced back.

00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:16.670
We found that the company had almost no online
presence whatsoever.

00:01:16.670 --> 00:01:23.020
Merely a single page website on one of those
website builders called cards with two RS,

00:01:23.020 --> 00:01:30.360
C, a, R, R, D, sort of like your website being
a political Praxis, political.blogspot.com

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:34.229
that's the equivalent of what they had and
it seemed weird.

00:01:34.229 --> 00:01:40.119
That's what we knew as of yesterday either
CBS hired a very shadowy company with almost

00:01:40.119 --> 00:01:46.880
no presence to file mass copyright claims
against left wing streamers or this was all

00:01:46.880 --> 00:01:52.099
a fraud and this company was claiming to represent
CBS when they did not.

00:01:52.099 --> 00:01:53.099
Now.

00:01:53.099 --> 00:01:55.289
Either way, the effect on us was disastrous.

00:01:55.289 --> 00:01:58.209
It put us at risk of a permanent ban from
Twitch.

00:01:58.209 --> 00:02:01.639
So I immediately contacted a lawyer, contacted
Twitch's legal department.

00:02:01.639 --> 00:02:04.579
I pointed out there's a lot of red flags here.

00:02:04.579 --> 00:02:09.930
I was notified late yesterday towards the
end of the day yesterday that Twitch's legal

00:02:09.930 --> 00:02:15.390
investigation determined the copyright strikes
were bogus.

00:02:15.390 --> 00:02:21.200
These scammers tricked Twitch into believing
that they represented CBS.

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:27.090
They did not, and they successfully got, I
don't know the number, a whole bunch of left

00:02:27.090 --> 00:02:28.920
wing streamers shut down.

00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:30.750
A number of articles have been written about
it.

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:33.790
This vice covered it, Newsweek covered it,
the verge covered it.

00:02:33.790 --> 00:02:36.530
There's a whole bunch of different articles
about it now.

00:02:36.530 --> 00:02:41.031
Additionally, while this investigation was
going on yesterday, the website for Praxis,

00:02:41.031 --> 00:02:45.530
political legal disappeared altogether from
the internet just removed.

00:02:45.530 --> 00:02:47.790
Very, very odd.

00:02:47.790 --> 00:02:53.470
So the right thing was done here in the sense
that they determined the strikes were bogus.

00:02:53.470 --> 00:02:56.530
They weren't from someone actually representing
CBS.

00:02:56.530 --> 00:02:58.660
They removed the strike from our account.

00:02:58.660 --> 00:03:00.410
Our account on Twitch has been reinstated.

00:03:00.410 --> 00:03:02.100
That's the good news.

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:04.950
The bad news is, and this is not getting enough
attention.

00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:13.920
The bad news is the broken dysfunctional system
that exists on both YouTube and Twitch for

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:20.590
dealing with copyright issues because both
YouTube and Twitch have a system where anybody

00:03:20.590 --> 00:03:27.120
claiming that, uh, their copyright is being
violated can almost instantly have live streams

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:28.870
and videos taken down.

00:03:28.870 --> 00:03:34.860
And then it becomes the responsibility of
the publisher, me, us to prove that either

00:03:34.860 --> 00:03:40.500
the claim was fraudulent, that we were authorized
because we have a license or fair use or whatever

00:03:40.500 --> 00:03:43.430
to broadcast or publish that content.

00:03:43.430 --> 00:03:47.270
It's sort of ban now, ask questions later.

00:03:47.270 --> 00:03:49.490
And this can take 24 hours.

00:03:49.490 --> 00:03:52.130
It could take 48 hours, it can take 30 days.

00:03:52.130 --> 00:03:59.830
It can sometimes take months because that
is how long YouTube keeps copyright strikes

00:03:59.830 --> 00:04:02.709
on until they eventually fall off on Twitch.

00:04:02.709 --> 00:04:04.280
They never fall off.

00:04:04.280 --> 00:04:07.070
Although there's rumors that they're looking
at changing that.

00:04:07.070 --> 00:04:12.310
So the right outcome ultimately prevailed
here, but it's a broken system.

00:04:12.310 --> 00:04:18.180
The system, you know, I, I was thinking about
Trump and the founding fathers hear me out.

00:04:18.180 --> 00:04:23.849
The founding fathers set up checks and balances
and they never imagined that a president would

00:04:23.849 --> 00:04:28.639
come in and simply ignore the checks and balances
which Donald Trump has done.

00:04:28.639 --> 00:04:29.639
And then what happens?

00:04:29.639 --> 00:04:30.639
It turns out nothing happens.

00:04:30.639 --> 00:04:34.990
There've been no consequences to Donald Trump
for flouting norms and checks and balances.

00:04:34.990 --> 00:04:41.669
The creators of YouTube and Twitch may never
have imagined that bad faith fraudulent actors

00:04:41.669 --> 00:04:42.949
would show up.

00:04:42.949 --> 00:04:47.539
While an important event for our democracy
is taking place, a presidential debate and

00:04:47.539 --> 00:04:54.990
file a massive number of bogus copyright claims
effectively shutting down endless, uh, of

00:04:54.990 --> 00:04:59.669
the, the viewership for thousands and tens
of thousands of people that were watching

00:04:59.669 --> 00:05:00.669
these streams.

00:05:00.669 --> 00:05:03.409
So the system has to be changed.

00:05:03.409 --> 00:05:07.490
They should have to show that their copyright
is being violated.

00:05:07.490 --> 00:05:11.759
They must have to prove that they are actually
authorized representatives of the copyright

00:05:11.759 --> 00:05:17.930
holder because otherwise, even though in this
one instance it was quote solved, the same

00:05:17.930 --> 00:05:24.029
thing will happen either next week or next
month or whenever we're covering events important

00:05:24.029 --> 00:05:29.389
to our democracy and it will continue to jeopardize
the livelihood of independent media creators

00:05:29.389 --> 00:05:30.460
like us.

00:05:30.460 --> 00:05:34.580
Ban first ask questions later, which is employed
by YouTube.

00:05:34.580 --> 00:05:35.580
It's employed by Twitch.

00:05:35.580 --> 00:05:36.710
It doesn't work.

00:05:36.710 --> 00:05:37.710
It doesn't work.

00:05:37.710 --> 00:05:42.659
And if anything, what we've learned from this
is, okay, if everybody gets together and spends

00:05:42.659 --> 00:05:48.800
almost 24 consecutive hours researching and
doing our own investigations and hiring our

00:05:48.800 --> 00:05:53.169
own lawyers, we can get one strike reversed.

00:05:53.169 --> 00:05:58.509
But this doesn't change the system that is
so acutely broken.

00:05:58.509 --> 00:06:01.979
Uh, and that's what we, we need to focus on
one way or the other.

00:06:01.979 --> 00:07:01.550
I don't know how to

00:07:01.550 --> 00:07:59.439
do it.

